1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:08,479
Coding agents, 60 seconds: why do you lose hours, never stop pasting your code, but how can 1 agent loop 4 steps until you're done?

2
00:00:08,979 --> 00:00:11,344
A chat assistant is the mechanic on the phone.

3
00:00:11,644 --> 00:00:12,738
He can only talk.

4
00:00:13,038 --> 00:00:16,487
So you paste his fix, run it, and carry the error back to him.

5
00:00:16,787 --> 00:00:17,682
Again and again.

6
00:00:18,632 --> 00:00:21,903
A coding agent is the mechanic in your garage, with tools.

7
00:00:22,203 --> 00:00:24,969
You give it one job, in your terminal or your editor.

8
00:00:25,269 --> 00:00:26,355
Then it works in a loop.

9
00:00:26,655 --> 00:00:27,792
It reads your files.

10
00:00:28,092 --> 00:00:29,066
It edits the code.

11
00:00:29,366 --> 00:00:31,214
It runs a command, and checks the result.

12
00:00:31,514 --> 00:00:32,377
Still broken?

13
00:00:32,677 --> 00:00:35,152
It goes around again, until the job is done.

14
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:38,822
That whole visit, every step and every result, is one session.

15
00:00:39,322 --> 00:00:40,746
You stop being the messenger.

16
00:00:41,046 --> 00:00:43,123
You watch, and you can stop it at any moment.

17
00:00:44,073 --> 00:00:46,501
It can still be wrong, so give it a test to run.

18
00:00:46,801 --> 00:00:48,038
But notice what changed.

19
00:00:48,338 --> 00:00:50,218
The mechanic did not get a bigger brain.

20
00:00:50,518 --> 00:00:52,891
He got hands, and a way to check his own work.

21
00:00:53,191 --> 00:00:54,755
That is what makes it an agent.

22
00:00:55,255 --> 00:00:56,657
Subscribe for the next one.
